  "idea": "Zapier vs Make.com: price comparison and complex scenario limits",
  "text": "Zapier versus Make: which platform should you build your core business on? Zapier connects over seven thousand apps, making it great for quick, simple marketing integrations. However, its rigid linear flow struggles when complex workflows require custom filters and error rollback. Make delivers complete flexibility with visual canvas routing, variable mapping, and live execution inspection. Use Zapier for basic triggers and Make for backend infrastructure.",
